  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nMid level ridging will continue until a short wave lifts out of the\nmid Mississippi Valley and crosses the region Tuesday night into\nWednesday. Flow will then become primarily zonal until late in the \nweek when some short wave ridging may develop as flow buckles with \nthe approach of a more significant short wave. \n\nSurface high pressure will prevail through Thursday with the low\nlevel flow veering over time. System passing across the upper Great\nLakes into New England will cause a front to lay out and sag across\nthe area Thursday night into Friday. There will be some increase in\nmoisture along the boundary but likely not sufficient to generate any\nprecipitation. Mid and high clouds will increase on Saturday as the\nnext system approach from the west southwest. \n\nHighs will be running 10 to 15 degrees above normal. Lows will also\nbe milder for the rest of the week with readings nearly 10 degrees\nabove normal. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nEnsemble systems in general agreement in bringing a short wave across\nthe area Sunday into Sunday night although there is spread in\namplitude. This will be accompanied by deeper moisture, so rain will\ndevelop into the area, possibly late Saturday night, but mostly\nfocused on Sunday. Some rain could linger into Monday, depending on \nthe location and strength of a trailing trough.",
